\f0\fs24 \cf0 \{"id":"0704.1461","submitter":"M. T. Yamashita",\
"authors":"M. T. Yamashita, T. Frederico and Lauro Tomio",\
"title":"Trajectory of neutron$-$neutron$-^\{18\}C$ excited three-body state",\
"comments":null,\
"journal-ref":"Phys.Lett.B660:339-344,2008",\
"doi":"10.1016/j.physletb.2008.01.008",\
"report-no":null,\
"categories":"nucl-th cond-mat.soft nucl-ex",\
"license":null,\
"abstract":"  The trajectory of the first excited Efimov state is investigated by using a\\nrenormalized zero-range three-body model for a system with two bound and one\\nvirtual two-body subsystems. The approach is applied to $n-n-^\{18\}$C, where the\\n$n-n$ virtual energy and the three-body ground state are kept fixed. It is\\nshown that such three-body excited state goes from a bound to a virtual state\\nwhen the $n-^\{18\}$C binding energy is increased. Results obtained for the\\n$n-^\{19\}$C elastic cross-section at low energies also show dominance of an\\n$S-$matrix pole corresponding to a bound or virtual Efimov state. It is also\\npresented a brief discussion of these findings in the context of ultracold atom\\nphysics with tunable scattering lengths.\\n",\
"versions":[\{"version":"v1","created":"Wed, 11 Apr 2007 17:38:36 GMT"\},\{"version":"v2","created":"Thu, 4 Oct 2007 22:19:23 GMT"\},\{"version":"v3","created":"Wed, 17 Oct 2007 11:50:47 GMT"\},\{"version":"v4","created":"Fri, 16 Nov 2007 19:44:13 GMT"\}],\
"update_date":"2011-03-28",\
"authors_parsed":[["Yamashita","M. T.",""],["Frederico","T.",""],["Tomio","Lauro",""]]\}\
